# xb1b.com — agent constraints

## Product

- Personal site at xb1b.com (formerly bibeka.com.np): single viewport-locked landing page with name "BIBEK / ARYAL".
- Two projects are linked, quietly, at the foot of the page: tithi.xb1b.com and brahma.xb1b.com. They are separate deployments.
- Contact is the email only (contact@xb1b.com), at the foot with the projects. No GitHub link on the page.
- Owner facts for SEO/GEO live in `lib/site.ts`; keep them true.
- No backend, no database, no Supabase, no auth, no forms unless explicitly requested.
- Do not reintroduce `/projects`, `/echo`, `/click`, or similar multi-page portfolio features without an explicit ask.

## Stack

- Next.js App Router + React + Tailwind + custom CSS for landing.
- Static-export-friendly / DB-free by default. Flag before adding a backend or DB.

## Visual

- Black night-sky background with a left-to-right Milky Way lavender glow band, white text.
- Name covers ~80–90% of the viewport on all screen sizes; page must not scroll (`100dvh`/`100svh`, overflow hidden).
- Subtle above all. Sky of tool/technology icons as distant stars: mostly dark, each slowly lighting up and going out; a few large, most small. Only tools Bibek actually uses. Icons sit behind the name with a mask so they do not overlay the text.
- No orbiting or circling text around the name.
- Favicon / app icons: white letter "B" on black.
- Font stack: `"Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif` (system; do not ship proprietary font files).

## Docs

- Keep `docs/` accurate when setup, architecture, or deploy steps change.
- This `.mdc` is agent constraints; `docs/` is human explanation — one fact, one owner.
